    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2020-october/q1",
      "question": "<p>The table below shows corresponding values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{1+x}}\"></span></p><p>The values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> are given to 4 significant figures.</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span></td><td>0.5</td><td>1</td><td>1.5</td><td>2</td><td>2.5</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span></td><td>0.5774</td><td>0.7071</td><td>0.7746</td><td>0.8165</td><td>0.8452</td></tr></table><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Use the trapezium rule, with all the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> in the table, to find an estimate for<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{0.5}^{2.5}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{1+x}}\\,\\mathrm dx\" data-display=\"true\"></div>giving your answer to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Using your answer to part (a), deduce an estimate for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_{0.5}^{2.5}\\sqrt{\\frac{9x}{1+x}}\\,\\mathrm dx\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{0.5}^{2.5}\\sqrt{\\frac{9x}{1+x}}\\,\\mathrm dx=4.535\\ \\text{to 4 significant figures}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>comment on the accuracy of your answer to part (b). <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
