      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2020-october/q8",
      "question": "<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(x)=6x^2+ax-23\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant</li><li>the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> intercept of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-12\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+4)\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\"></span></li></ul><p>find, in simplest form, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
