    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2020-october/q9",
      "question": "<p>A quantity of ethanol was heated until it reached boiling point.</p><p>The temperature of the ethanol, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds after heating began, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta=A-B\\mathrm e^{-0.07t}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are positive constants.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the initial temperature of the ethanol was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span></li><li>after 10 seconds the temperature of the ethanol was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"44\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find a complete equation for the model, giving the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>Ethanol has a boiling point of approximately <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"78\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use this information to evaluate the model. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
