      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2020-october/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: a V-shaped graph with vertex P below the x-axis to the left of the y-axis; the right branch crosses the y-axis above the origin O.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the graph with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2\\left|x+4\\right|-5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The vertex of the graph is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, shown in Figure 2.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Solve the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x+40=2\\left|x+4\\right|-5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>A line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=ax\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\left|x+4\\right|-5\"></span> at least once,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>find the range of possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, writing your answer in set notation. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
